             fma:FMAID "24875" ;
             fma:definition "Limb segment which is distal to the limb girdle and demarcated by the plane of the surfaces of the glenoid and acetabular fossae from the limb girdle; together with the limb girdle, it constitutes the limb. Examples: There are only four instances, right and left free upper limbs and right and left free lower limbs." ;
             fma:preferred_name "Free limb" ;
             rdfs:label "Free limb"@en .

