###  http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma67498
fma:fma67498 rdf:type owl:Class ;
             rdfs:subClassOf fma:fma67135 ;
             fma:FMAID "67498" ;
             fma:definition "Anatomical structure which has as its direct parts portions of two or more types of tissue or two or more types of cardinal organ part which constitute a maximally connected anatomical structure demarcated predominantly by a bona fide anatomical surface. Examples: femur, biceps brachii, liver, heart, skin, tracheobronchial tree, ovary." ;
             fma:non-English_equivalent "Organe" ,
